october is breast cancer awareness month  it's estimated one in eight women will  get that dreaded diagnosis so in today's  buddy check a report denise valdez tells  us the step you should take to find the  right doctor if you ever get that  diagnosis  recently breastcancer.org talked to  three doctors oncologists and surgeons  who had breast cancer the role is kind  of reversed for them they got to see  what it was like to be a patient but  then they also learned a few things in  finding the right cancer team for them i  call myself  a dual citizen  a doctor and a patient  breastcancer.org founder and chief  medical officer marissa weiss sharing  observations with other physicians on  their breast cancer journey i learned  that  the doctor-patient relationship is so  sacred  i mean  you are really trusting someone to  protect and cherish your life and your  life is your greatest gift each expert  recommends meeting with a few doctors if  you can ask for referrals read reviews  and come prepared upon that initial  meeting someone who has the expertise  the judgment the knowledge the  experience that you need in order to get  the best care possible the best care  means the greatest benefits and the  least side effects a doctor who listens  to you hears you takes you seriously and  will help get you back to the person you  were before the diagnosis the only way  that i was going to get the care that i  needed was to advocate for myself to  find my voice to speak up although it's  a club none of them wanted to be in they  came out the other side with a better  understanding of what it's like to be a  patient and a survivor for buddy check  denise valdez live local now
 

